d measure offsets. System must be reliable and novice-friendly.\n\n### Timeline\n\n- **Now → end of April**: commit field-validated fixes, daily water tests\n- **May** (~2 weeks effective — Roland away 2 weeks): Kongsberg M3 sonar integration, camera costmap work\n- **June**: class begins\n\n## Milestones\n\n### 1. Commit \u0026 merge field-validated fixes\n\nToday's water test (2026-04-16) validated three critical fixes that are live on gabby but not yet committed to repos:\n\n- [x] Commit CrabbingPathFollower PID YAML with correct PidROS key names (`p: -20.0, i: -0.5, d: -0.6`) — echoboat config landed; class-relevant scope is bizzyboat only (echoboat config), so no further audit required\n- [x] Backport hover.cpp v4 patch (range-aware minimum speed + cliff at minimum_radius) to `unh_marine_navigation` repo\n- [ ] Log and commit TF extrapolation fix for multi-line survey goals (stale `header.stamp` on per-line goals) — still needs investigating\n- [x] Merge gitcloud field fixes to origin (chart datum, network monitor, params) — `make sync` confirmed all 32 repos in sync 2026-04-23\n- [ ] Apply FCU battery params (#55) to Cube at boat, then merge PR #56 — field-gated\n\n### 2. Kongsberg M3 sonar integration\n\nLoaner M3 multibeam arriving ~2026-04-17. Windows PC (mercat) runs acquisition software.\n\n- [ ] Configure mercat NTP (w32tm) — Meinberg `ntpd` running against TM2000B; pending final verification of sync quality\n- [x] Network integration — intentionally simple for loaner: direct Ethernet from M3 to a spare mercat port, keeping M3's factory static IP (192.168.1.234). No DHCP reservation or DNS name needed at this scope.\n- [ ] ROS coverage visualization — early planning only; idea is QINSy → ROS bridge (marine_tools#1); nothing implemented or tested yet\n- [ ] Measure and configure sensor offsets (URDF update for M3 mount position) — measurements captured 2026-04-22 for SBG/SVS/M3 (`hydro_payload_install_log.md`); URDF update still pending\n\n### 3. Camera costmap \u0026 obstacle avoidance\n\n- [ ] Fix `SeaSurfaceLayer::matchSize()` segfault in controller_server (workaround: remove from local costmap plugins)\n- [x] Reduce UDP bridge camera bandwidth defaults — commits b00f4ad, 0b7a558, 3c4aaec, 7ee3947, e5af89f moved OAKs to H.265 with tuned bitrates (1000–2000 kbps) and mirrored over the VPN bridge\n- [x] Per-connection traffic diagnostics for udp_bridge (rolker/udp_bridge#7, PR rolker/udp_bridge#8) — merged 2026-04-20\n- [ ] Validate OAK camera → costmap pipeline end-to-end — blocked on the `SeaSurfaceLayer` segfault fix above\n\n### 4. Class-ready polish\n\n- [x] Annunciator: stale indicators now escalate to WARN/ERROR instead of grey — rolker/rqt_operator_tools#16 merged 2026-04-20 (panel-side fix; supersedes the node-side republish-cached proposal for this UX problem)\n- [x] Annunciator: fix `_handle_diagnostics` value-extraction fallback (Starlink shows serial instead of status) — addressed by rolker/starlink_stats_ros#5 rework 2026-04-16\n- [x] Annunciator: `starlink_diagnostics_node` populate `status.message` with readable summary — rolker/starlink_stats_ros#5 adds per-task `status.message`\n- [x] Annunciator: show RTK fix type (none/float/fixed) in GPS entry instead of satellite count (#61) — PR #64 merged 2026-04-20\n- [x] Annunciator: add NTRIP correction stream status (#60) — PR #64 merged 2026-04-20\n- [x] Annunciator: add UDP bridge link status (#62) — PR #63 merged 2026-04-20\n- [ ] Pre-launch checklist (rqt plugin or printed reference)\n- [ ] Operator logbook (rqt plugin) — Phase 1 implementation landed in rolker/rqt_operator_tools#2, **not yet field-tested** so not considered done\n- [ ] Student-facing operating documentation\n- [ ] Formal WiFi range test (deferred) — 2026-04-21 field data shows graceful degradation well past the old \"300 m limit\" and range comparable to or better than 2025 IzzyBoat; captured in memory (`project_wifi_range.md`). A dedicated range test is a future task, not class-prep scope.\n\n### Lower priority / deferred\n\n- Hover v5 (range-aware taper for faster excursion recovery) — v4 is sufficient\n- Hover vectored-thrust parameter — works well enough with v4 cliff\n- DNS-over-HTTPS on RUTX11\n- WiFi bridge: static routes → default gateway approach\n- Forward USB camera (black image)\n- IzzyBoat WireGuard return path fix\n\n## Deployment Log\n\nContinues from the running log in `docs/bizzyboat_deployment_log.md` (2263 lines covering 2026-03-26 through 2026-04-16).\n\n## References\n\n- Parent deployment: #14 (closed)\n- Previous field ops: #43 (closed, merged via PR #54)\n- Deployment guide: #18 (open, WIP draft committed)\n- FCU battery params: #55 / PR #56\n- NTP investigation: #45 / PR #46\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1776387419,"nonce":"Ec5tlIGRUN1on/hl0rNZrjrpsQU=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM7-LtB0","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/57#issuecomment-4264480884"},"message":"Adding items based on planning session:\n\n**mercat (Windows PC)**:\n- [ ] Enable SSH on mercat for remote debugging and configuration\n- [ ] Configure NTP (w32tm or Meinberg) — TM2000B as primary, boat router as fallback\n- [ ] Investigate PTP support on TM2000B — if supported, could achieve \u003c100μs sync vs w32tm's ~100ms\n\n**M3 sonar note**: The Kongsberg M3 is from the Mesotech product line (acquired company), NOT the EM series. The `kongsberg_em` / `kd-em-ros-controller` ROS packages likely don't apply. Need to investigate the M3's actual data protocol and interface when hardware arrives.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1776387789,"nonce":"BSk33Ih7g5X8DlYuKtzrXygcFdg=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM7-L2H6","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/57#issuecomment-4264518138"},"message":"## PTP time sync research\n\nThe TM2000B (192.168.20.123) supports **IEEE 1588:2008 PTP** — multicast and unicast, 50+ devices.\n\n### Upgrade path\n\n| Machine | Current | PTP option | Expected accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| gabby | chrony NTP (~1ms) | `ptp4l` + `phc2sys` (linuxptp, Ubuntu 24.04) | ~10-100μs |\n| mercat | not configured | Native Windows PTP (needs PTP-capable NIC) or Meinberg | NIC-dependent |\n| salmon | chrony NTP (~1ms) | Could add PTP, lower priority | — |\n\n### Constraints\n\n- **PoE switch (Trendnet TI-PG80B) is unmanaged** — no transparent/boundary clock. PTP still works but degrades from sub-μs to ~10-100μs. Still much better than NTP.\n- **Windows native PTP** (W10 v1909+) requires a NIC with hardware timestamping support (Intel I217-V, I219-V work; I350 does not). Need to check mercat's NIC.\n- **Meinberg NTP client** is the fallback for mercat if PTP isn't viable — achieves ~10ms vs w32tm's ~100ms.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nPTP on gabby (linuxptp) is highest value — ROS 2 timestamps originate there. mercat NTP/PTP depends on NIC and whether the M3 has its own time source.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1776390455,"nonce":"UGFnwRm7onIJ3+lfRg8RimPupgI=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM7-MlPn","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/57#issuecomment-4264711143"},"message":"## M3 Sonar — research findings and integration plan\n\n### Protocol (now understood)\n\n- **Control**: TCP XML API on port 20001 — commands like `Connect`, `Start_Ping`, `Start_Export`\n- **Data**: Proprietary IMB binary format (sync words 0x8000 x4, PacketHeader, DataHeader with per-ping nav/attitude/beam angles, DataBody with beamformed samples, PacketFooter)\n- **File formats**: `.imb` (beamformed, primary), `.mmb` (raw element), `.all` (EM datagram export for MB-System/CARIS/HYPACK)\n- **Nav input**: External position/attitude via UDP or serial\n- **Time sync**: NMEA ZDA on UDP port 31100 at 1 Hz for 1PPS\n\n### Existing ROS 2 driver\n\n[vortexntnu/vortex-m3-sonar-driver](https://github.com/vortexntnu/vortex-m3-sonar-driver) — complete C++ driver that connects to M3 via TCP, parses IMB binary, publishes `PointCloud2`. `ImbFormat.hpp` is a full reverse-engineered spec of the IMB format.\n\n### Integration plan — refined\n\nData should flow through `cube_bathymetry` using `marine_acoustic_msgs`:\n\n```\nM3 sonar → M3 software (mercat) → TCP → M3 ROS 2 driver (gabby)\n    → marine_acoustic_msgs/RawSonarImage or SonarDetections\n    → cube_bathymetry → grid_map → coverage viz (CAMP)\n```\n\n**Work needed**:\n1. Adapt Vortex driver to publish `marine_acoustic_msgs` (RawSonarImage and/or SonarDetections) instead of raw PointCloud2. IMB DataHeader has beam angles, frequency, sound speed, sample rate — maps cleanly to the message fields.\n2. Verify `cube_bathymetry` can consume M3 data (may need tuning beyond DeltaT defaults)\n3. Nav feed: publish NMEA position/heading from gabby → M3 software via UDP\n4. Time sync: NMEA ZDA on UDP 31100 from TM2000B\n5. Configure `.all` export for MB-System post-processing pipeline\n\n### Third-party support\n\nMB-System reads `.all` export (format 58). QINSy has a dedicated M3 driver. CARIS/HYPACK/Echoview also supported.\n\n### mercat setup\n\n- [ ] Enable SSH for remote debugging\n- [ ] NTP/PTP for time sync (see PTP comment above)\n- [ ] DHCP reservation already done (192.168.20.8)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1776792206,"nonce":"Fujf7Luy02/lZ9yqqKI5LDcwxwo=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM7_vAxi","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/57#issuecomment-4290514018"},"message":"Adding cross-reference: sonar data ingestion from Qinsy (running on mercat for M3) into the ROS pipeline is tracked in rolker/marine_tools#1 — \"Add QPS Qinsy UDP bridge node for ingesting processed soundings.\"\n\nThis is the mechanism for the \"ROS coverage visualization\" item under Milestone 2.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1776796403,"nonce":"7mSuYHTu3Jx2rqBfpPqL9JWb5xU=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM7_wjLv","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/57#issuecomment-4290917103"},"message":"Adding cross-reference: the direct M3 ROS 2 driver (`.all` bathymetry + IMB water column) is tracked in rolker/marine_tools#2.\n\nThis is the second path for M3 sonar integration (alongside rolker/marine_tools#1 for the Qinsy bridge). Both feed into the bathymetry pipeline but at different entry points — the direct driver provides raw detections via `SonarDetections`, while the Qinsy bridge provides processed soundings with TPU.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1777295552,"nonce":"GvmejtSEAukBFZm7bsikarVCNdw=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM7_DjmqzwAAAAXMkGyw"},"status":2},{"type":3,"timestamp":1777295607,"nonce":"fCiJSlVaXl3n9zDdt8kjS5EzhTQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAeyWug","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/57#issuecomment-4327249594"},"message":"Closing this umbrella in favor of the per-(deployment, host) logging convention introduced in #92 / merged via [PR #93](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/93).\n\n**Where the open work landed**\n\n| #57 item | Now tracked at |\n| --- | --- |\n| TF extrapolation on multi-line survey goals | [`rolker/unh_marine_navigation#23`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/23) |\n| `SeaSurfaceLayer::matchSize()` segfault | [`rolker/unh_marine_perception#6`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/6) |\n| OAK→costmap end-to-end validation | [`rolker/unh_marine_perception#7`](https://github.com/r